 AI labs and cloud partners will NVIDIA disclose at its next annual report?'), ('clean-2', 'How much will NVIDIA disclose in purchase and supply commitments (obligations to buy capacity, components or services) at its next annual report?'), ('clean-3', 'Will Nvidia be permitted to sell its current Blackwell-generation AI chips into China — through U.S. export approval and Chinese acceptance of shipments — by the end of fiscal 2027?'), ('clean-4', \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, which the company says has entered full production, reach volume customer shipments (first revenue recognition) by the end of fiscal 2027?\"), ('clean-5', 'How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data centers in calendar 2026?')]\nARTICLE 7 NAMED [{'figure': 1, 'text': 'about 70% revenue growth guided for fiscal 2028'}, {'figure': 2, 'text': 'the margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028'}] QUESTIONS [('clean-1', 'What total of credit support and minimum-revenue guarantees to AI labs and cloud partners will NVIDIA disclose at its next annual report?'), ('clean-2', 'How much will NVIDIA disclose in purchase and supply commitments (obligations to buy capacity, components or services) at its next annual report?'), ('clean-3', 'Will Nvidia be permitted to sell its current Blackwell-generation AI chips into China — through U.S. export approval and Chinese acceptance of shipments — by the end of fiscal 2027?'), ('clean-4', \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, which the company says has entered full production, reach volume customer shipments (first revenue recognition) by the end of fiscal 2027?\"), ('clean-5', 'How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data centers in calendar 2026?')]\nTypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
