70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time; the stock rose roughly 7% after the earnings report. | Nvidia (results and guidance); analysts (prior expectation) | None | [(1, 'Revenue growth', 'more than doubled', 'actual', 'Nvidia (results and guidance); analysts (prior expectation)'), (2, 'Revenue growth guidance', '70%', 'guidance', 'Nvidia (results and guidance); analysts (prior expectation)'), (3, 'Revenue growth expectation', '45%', 'estimate', 'Nvidia (results and guidance); analysts (prior expectation)')] | none\n\n B27 ARTICLE 7\nev-1 | NVIDIA management expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company's history, and sizes NVIDIA's revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell. | NVIDIA management | None | [(1, 'revenue opportunity per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin', 'about $40 billion per gigawatt', 'estimate', 'NVIDIA management')] | ['clean-4']\nev-3 | NVIDIA management guided to about 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028 — the first time it has guided a full year ahead — with the CEO saying demand is much greater than 70% and that supply is what holds the guide there. | NVIDIA management (CEO) | None | [(1, 'revenue growth', 'about 70%', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA management (CEO)')] | none\nev-5 | NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs, part of a demand picture the article says leans on NVIDIA's own balance sheet; management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'investment in frontier AI labs', 'nearly $50 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-1']\nev-6 | NVIDIA guided its gross margin lower, to settle in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, as memory prices rose more than management expected, partly offset by price increases NVIDIA has already executed. | NVIDIA management | None | [(1, '