'estimate', 'Bloomberg (compiled analyst estimates)')] | ['clean-2']\n\n B33 ARTICLE 8\ne1 | NVIDIA's fiscal 2026 (year ended January 2026) revenue reached nearly $215.9 billion, up roughly 65.5% year over year, producing net income of approximately $120.1 billion and a net margin of approximately 55.6%, consistent with the 55.8% net margin of the prior fiscal year, according to Fool.com's comparison article. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'revenue', 'nearly $215.9 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (2, 'revenue growth year over year', 'roughly 65.5%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (3, 'net income', 'approximately $120.1 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (4, 'net margin', 'approximately 55.6%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ABSENT\ne2 | NVIDIA's total revenue more than doubled year over year in its latest reported quarter, with almost all of it coming from data center customers, and its data center business generated $89 billion in that quarter alone, per Fool.com. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'data center revenue', '$89 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ABSENT\ne3 | NVIDIA management guided its next quarter to $108 billion of revenue, with an outlook that assumes no data center compute sales to China at all (excluding any China compute sales), as reported by Fool.com. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'revenue guidance', '$108 billion', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA')] | ABSENT\ne4 | NVIDIA recently agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion to expand its software capabilities, as reported by Fool.com; the item does not say the transaction has closed. | NVIDIA | recently | [(1, 'acquisition consideration for Hugging Face', 'approximately $12.9 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ABSENT\ne5 | NVIDIA disclosed that sales to two direct customers represented 22% and 14% of total revenue in fiscal 2026, respectively, a customer concentration the article flags as a risk. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'sales to largest direct customer as share of total revenue', '22%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (2, 'sales to second direct customer as share of total revenue', '14%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ABSENT\n\n B40 ARTICLE 10\nev-1 | On NVIDIA's fiscal Q2 2027 earnings call, management said inventory rose to $32 billion as the company prepared for the Vera Rubin launch. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'inventory', '$32 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-4']\nev-2 | NVIDIA management guided fiscal Q3 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, while the consensus forecast for that quarter is $111.3 billion, above the top of that guidance range. | NVIDIA (guidance); consensus estimate as reported by Trefis | None | [(1, 'revenue guidance', '$108 billion', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA (guidance); consensus estimate as reported by Trefis'), (2, 'consensus revenue forecast', '$111.3 billion', 'estimate', 'NVIDIA (guidance); consensus estimate as reported by Trefis')] | none\nev-3 | NVIDIA management said fiscal Q2 2027 revenue was $96 billion, more than double the year-earlier figure, with growth accelerating for the fourth consecutive quarter. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'revenue', '$96 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | none\nev-4 | NVIDIA guided gross margin for fiscal Q3 2027 to 74%, plus or minus half a point, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027, with management pointing to higher component costs, especially memory. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'gross margin guidance', '74%', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA'), (2, 'gross margin', '75%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | none\nev-5 | NVIDIA management expects the newly launched Vera Rubin platform to make up about 20% of its data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'Vera Rubin share of data center revenue', 'about 20%', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-4']\nev-7 | Trefis reports that NVIDIA's operating margin is 65%, its highest in ten years, against a three-year average of 59%. | Trefis (analysis of NVIDIA reported figures) | None | [(1, 'operating margin', '65%', 'actual', 'Trefis (analysis of NVIDIA reported figures)'), (2, 'operating margin, three-year average', '59%', 'a