pect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year, Fool.com reported. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'revenue growth', 'roughly 70%', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA')] | none\ne3 | NVIDIA guided to $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'revenue', '$108 billion', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA'), (2, 'sequential revenue growth', '17%', 'guidance', 'NVIDIA')] | none\ne4 | NVIDIA's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, with receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July and days sales outstanding rising from 45 to 60 days in one quarter; NVIDIA said it extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers, which the article flags as a sign customers are taking longer to pay. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'total assets growth', 'more than 50%', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (2, 'accounts receivable', '$38.5 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (3, 'accounts receivable', '$63.1 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA'), (4, 'days sales outstanding (DSO)', '45 to 60 days', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-1']\ne5 | NVIDIA agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI, cited by Fool.com as part of a string of 'circular' financial moves in which NVIDIA helps customers pay for its products; the item gives no date for the agreement. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'guarantee of OpenAI data center lease obligations', 'up to $105 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-1']\ne6 | NVIDIA has formed partnerships to raise over $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure, according to Fool.com, which cites this alongside the OpenAI lease guarantee as evidence NVIDIA is helping customers pay for its products; the item gives no date or partner names. | NVIDIA | None | [(1, 'outside capital raised for AI infrastructure through partnerships', 'over $500 billion', 'actual', 'NVIDIA')] | ['clean-1']\n\n B56 ARTICLE 9\nev-1 | Zacks Consensus Estimates project Nvidia's upcoming-quarter EPS at $2.47, a 90.00% increase versus the same quarter a year earlier, and revenue at $109.02 billion, a 91.24% increase versus the year-ago quarter, according to the latest consensus cited by Zacks. | Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates) | 2026-09-28 | [(1, 'EPS', '$2.47', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates)'), (2, 'Revenue', '$109.02 billion', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates)')] | none\nev-2 | Zacks Consensus Estimates project Nvidia's full-year earnings at $9.25 per share and revenue at $406.05 billion, which would represent increases of 93.92% and 88.04%, respectively, from the prior year. | Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates) | 2026-09-28 | [(1, 'Earnings per share', '$9.25 per share', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates)'), (2, 'Revenue', '$406.05 billion', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates)')] | none\nev-3 | The Zacks Consensus EPS estimate for Nvidia has been revised 4.73% upward over the past month, per Zacks. | Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates) | 2026-09-28 | [(1, 'Zacks Consensus EPS estimate revision', '4.73%', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimates)')] | none\n\n B58 ARTICLE 9\ne1 | The Zacks Consensus Estimates cited in the article project Nvidia's upcoming-quarter EPS at $2.47, a 90.00% increase versus the same quarter a year earlier, and upcoming-quarter revenue at $109.02 billion, a 91.24% increase versus the year-ago quarter. | Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research) | None | [(1, 'EPS (Zacks Consensus Estimate)', '$2.47', 'estimate', 'Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research)'), (2, 'revenue (Zacks Consensus Estimate)', '$109.02 billion', 'estimate', 'Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research)')] | none\ne2 | The Zacks Consensus Estimates cited in the article project Nvidia's full-year earnings at $9.25 per share, +93.92% versus the prior year, and full-year revenue at $406.05 billion, +88.04% versus the prior year. | Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research) | None | [(1, 'earnings per share (Zacks Consensus Estimate)', '$9.25 per share', 'estimate', 'Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research)'), (2, 'revenue (Zacks Consensus Estimate)', '$406.05 billion', 'estimate', 'Zacks Consensus Estimates (Zacks Investment Research)')] | none\ne3 | Zacks reports that its Consensus EPS estimate for Nvidia has been revised 4.73% upward over the past month, a direction it reads as analysts turning more positive on the near-term business, and that Nvidia currently carries a Zacks Rank of #1 (Strong Buy). | Zacks Investment Research | past month (relative date, as stated) | [(1, 'Zacks Consensus EPS estimate revision', '4.73%', 'estimate', 'Zacks Investment Research')] | none\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
